.TH S3M-LS 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-ls \- parallel bucket lister
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-ls
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fBs3://\fIBUCKET\fR[\fB/\fIPREFIX\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists objects in one or more buckets or prefixes with a pool of worker threads and emits every object found as CSV.
Parallelism comes from prefix sharding: delimiter listings discover the directory structure of the key space and each discovered prefix is listed concurrently.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " LEVEL"
Detail level.
\fBbasic\fR (default) prints the key; \fBstandard\fR adds size, mtime, etag and storage class; \fBfull\fR adds owner, content type, version id and server-side encryption, at the cost of one extra HEAD request per object.
\fBb\fR, \fBs\fR and \fBf\fR are accepted.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-class " CLASSES"
Only output objects of these storage classes (comma-separated, case-insensitive), for example \fB\-\-class STANDARD,GLACIER\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the output to FILE and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH OUTPUT
Output order is non-deterministic; pipe through
.BR sort (1)
for a stable order.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-du (1),
.BR s3m\-find (1)
